# SABOTAGE: T77 (spec §I4 "unfair advantage") — REGENERATED fix round 1 (context shifted:
# the wording rewrite + worst-of-N comment above this cond clause). Health-formula
# integrity: removes the `dunning?(status, pd) -> {dunning_value(pd),
# dunning_explanation(pd, status)}` clause from `Samen.Web.AccountHealth`'s billing factor
# `cond`. Without it, a book with ANY number of past-due subscriptions/invoices, at ANY
# overdue age, falls straight through to the `status in [:active, :trialing] -> {1.0, ...}`
# branch — the exact health/dunning incoherence `Samen.Web.Operator.HealthScore`
# (WS-B/ADR-019) was built to fix, reintroduced independently in this module's own
# (deliberately separate) formula. A book in deep dunning (max-cap-eligible: 90+ days
# overdue) would score a PERFECT billing dimension (1.0) and the composite would read
# "healthy" instead of "at risk" — precisely the lie a health score exists to prevent, AND
# (fix round 1) the same bug the WORST-OF-N fix closed at the status-selection layer would
# be reopened at the SCORING layer even with the correct worst status selected. Reverts
# byte-exact.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/crm_account_health_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: score/1: DUNNING CEILING caps the billing value even at max cap-eligible overdue age
# MUST_FAIL: snapshot/2: DUNNING wiring — a real past-due invoice caps the billing dimension end-to-end
# MUST_FAIL: snapshot/2 WORST-OF-N (fix round 1, MED-2): an active sub + a sibling past_due sub reports the WORST status, never the best one
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/account_health.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/account_health.ex
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/account_health.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/account_health.ex
@@ -297,9 +297,6 @@ defmodule Samen.Web.AccountHealth do
         status in [:cancelled, :canceled] ->
           {0.0, "at least one customer subscription is cancelled — treat as churn risk in this book"}
 
-        dunning?(status, pd) ->
-          {dunning_value(pd), dunning_explanation(pd, status)}
-
         status in [:active, :trialing] ->
           {1.0, "the worst subscription state on file is '#{status}' — current, no past-due invoices anywhere in the book"}
 
